Lodestone bundles and distributes the following third-party components. Each is
listed with its licence, the upstream project it comes from, and — where we had
to modify it to run on Android — the fork carrying those changes.

Every fork below sits on the exact upstream commit its released binary was built
from, with our patches as individual commits on the `lodestone/android-arm64`
branch, so the published source corresponds to the published binary.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OpenJDK  (java 8, 17, 21, 25)
    GPL-2.0 WITH Classpath-exception-2.0
    https://github.com/openjdk/jdk8u   -> https://github.com/lodestone-launcher/jdk8u
    https://github.com/openjdk/jdk17u  -> https://github.com/lodestone-launcher/jdk17u
    https://github.com/openjdk/jdk21u  -> https://github.com/lodestone-launcher/jdk21u
    https://github.com/openjdk/jdk25u  -> https://github.com/lodestone-launcher/jdk25u

    Modified. The Classpath exception is what allows Lodestone's own code to
    remain separately licensed while linking against the runtime; the runtime
    itself stays GPL, and its corresponding source is the tagged branch above.

Mesa  (Zink, Turnip, libdrm)
    MIT
    https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa
    -> https://github.com/lodestone-launcher/mesa

    Modified. That fork is a single-branch import of the mesa-26.1.6 tree rather
    than full history, because the upstream clone could not complete; GitLab
    remains canonical. The imported root tree hash matches upstream's for that
    tag and can be checked independently.

OpenAL Soft
    LGPL-2.1-or-later
    https://github.com/kcat/openal-soft, tag 1.23.1, commit d3875f333

    Unmodified. Cross-compiled for Android from that exact commit with no source
    changes, so upstream is the corresponding source. It ships as a separate
    shared library and is loaded dynamically, so it may be replaced with another
    build of the same version.

gl4es
    MIT
    https://github.com/ptitSeb/gl4es

    Unmodified. Built from the upstream default branch; see runtime/build-gl4es.sh.

LWJGL 3.3.3  (and its vendored stb and tinyfiledialogs)
    BSD-3-Clause
    https://github.com/LWJGL/lwjgl3

    Unmodified. Cross-compiled for Android; see runtime/build-lwjgl.sh.

FreeType
    FTL  (dual-licensed FTL / GPL-2.0; Lodestone takes the FTL)
    https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/freetype/freetype

    Unmodified. Portions of this software are copyright (c) The FreeType Project
    (www.freetype.org). All rights reserved.

libffi
    MIT
    https://github.com/libffi/libffi

    Unmodified. Linked into LWJGL's core native library.

LLVM libc++  (libc++_shared.so)
    Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
    https://llvm.org

    Unmodified, as shipped in the Android NDK.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Not third-party: app/src/main/cpp/mesa/hardware_stub.cpp is Lodestone's own
stand-in for Android's libhardware, which an unprivileged app cannot load. It is
not part of Mesa.

